---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import IndustryControlFlow from "../components/diagrams/IndustryControlFlow.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Financial Services | BeaconGuard Expansion Vertical"
  description="BeaconGuard authorizes whether financial applications may invoke AI and whether declared actions based on AI proposals may proceed. It does not determine fraud, AML, credit, or legal outcomes."
>
  <section class="stack-section">
    <p class="section-label">EXPANSION VERTICAL</p>
    <h1>
      Control proposed financial AI actions before they affect regulated
      systems.
    </h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Financial services is an expansion vertical after healthcare. BeaconGuard
      governs whether an application may invoke an AI provider and whether a
      declared enterprise action based on an AI-generated result may proceed.
      BeaconGuard authorizes use of a proposed result; customer analysts,
      models, and systems of record retain fraud, AML, credit, and legal
      determination ownership.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Financial governed AI transaction</h2>
    <p>
      Provider invocation is not the complete governed outcome. Case
      recommendations, escalations, customer communications, case-state
      changes, and fraud or dispute actions still require independent
      Result-to-Action Authorization of the declared intended action.
    </p>
    <IndustryControlFlow industry="financial" />
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What BeaconGuard authorizes — and what it does not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Authorizes:</strong> whether the application may invoke the AI
        provider under the Active Verified Release.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Authorizes:</strong> whether the declared intended enterprise
        action may proceed — for example, using a proposed recommendation,
        escalation, communication, or case-state change.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Does not determine:</strong> fraud, AML, KYC, credit, dispute,
        or legal outcomes. Customer analysts, models, and systems of record
        retain those judgments.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      AI-generated results remain untrusted proposals. Provider success is not
      enterprise authorization. Runtime outcomes are ALLOW or DENY only.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Existing financial systems remain in place</h2>
    <p>
      BeaconGuard does not replace case management, transaction systems,
      analyst authorization, model risk management, or compliance judgment.
      Those systems remain authoritative. BeaconGuard authorizes; the
      enterprise application executes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Financial scenarios</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Illustrative controlled example.</strong> Expansion scenarios.
      Each treats the AI result as an untrusted proposal whose declared use
      requires independent authorization.
    </p>
    <div class="scenario-grid">
      <div class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Proposed case recommendation</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Existing workflow:</strong> Analyst-assist request over case
          materials returns a recommended disposition.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI-Generated Result:</strong> Proposed recommendation —
          untrusted proposal.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Intended action:</strong> Apply or queue the recommended
          case disposition.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>BeaconGuard role:</strong> Authorizes admission and the
          declared use of the proposal — not the correctness of the AML or case
          determination.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Authoritative system:</strong> Case management remains
          authoritative.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Escalation</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Existing workflow:</strong> AI proposes escalating a case to
          a higher-risk queue or senior reviewer.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI-Generated Result:</strong> Escalation proposal — untrusted.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Intended action:</strong> Create or route the escalation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Result-to-Action:</strong> ALLOW or DENY for the declared
          escalation action under the Active Verified Release.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Authoritative system:</strong> Case and escalation platforms
          remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Customer communication</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Existing workflow:</strong> Customer-impacting message draft
          from an AI-assisted path.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI-Generated Result:</strong> Proposed customer communication
          — untrusted proposal.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Intended action:</strong> Send, queue, or suppress the
          communication.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Result-to-Action:</strong> Independent authorization of the
          declared communication action; DENY prevents enterprise effect.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Authoritative system:</strong> Customer operations and
          compliance remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Case-state change</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Existing workflow:</strong> AI proposes updating case status,
          ownership, or workflow stage.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI-Generated Result:</strong> Proposed state change —
          untrusted proposal.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Intended action:</strong> Update case state in the system of
          record.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>BeaconGuard role:</strong> Authorizes whether that declared
          state change may proceed — not the underlying risk determination.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Authoritative system:</strong> Case management remains
          authoritative.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Fraud or dispute action</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Existing workflow:</strong> Fraud or dispute investigation
          assist returns a proposed investigative or remediation action.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Request Admission:</strong> DENY on replay, freshness, or
          pathway failure before provider invocation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Intended action:</strong> Execute a declared fraud or dispute
          workflow action.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>BeaconGuard role:</strong> Authorizes use of the proposed
          result for the declared action — not the fraud, dispute, or legal
          determination itself.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Authoritative system:</strong> Fraud and dispute platforms
          remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What BeaconGuard does not claim</h2>
    <ul class="bg-nonclaim-list">
      <li>Fraud, AML, KYC, credit, or legal determination</li>
      <li>Replacement of analyst authorization or compliance judgment</li>
      <li>Replacement of case management or transaction systems</li>
      <li>Model risk management certification</li>
      <li>Production-ready or customer financial production validation</li>
      <li>Semantic authorization of model content as truth</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a
        class="btn-primary"
        href="mailto:architecture@beaconguardassurance.com?subject=Financial%20Workflow%20Review"
      >
        Request a Financial Workflow Review
      </a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/healthcare">Healthcare Initial Market</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/docs/architecture">Review System Architecture</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
